proof.text:
The equivalent transpose characterization in [def-weil-pbc-adjunction-mate], applied to $a=e^{-1}$ and the same adjunction on both sides, says
$$\varepsilon_{GM}\circ L(b_M)=G(\varepsilon_M)\circ a_{RM}.$$
For $(M,\psi)$, naturality of $\varepsilon$ for $\psi:GM\to M$ and cancellation of $a_{RM}\circ e_{RM}=1_{GLRM}$ now give
$$\begin{aligned}
\varepsilon_M\circ L(s_M)\circ e_{RM}
&=\varepsilon_M\circ LR(\psi)\circ L(b_M)\circ e_{RM}\\
&=\psi\circ\varepsilon_{GM}\circ L(b_M)\circ e_{RM}
=\psi\circ G(\varepsilon_M).
\end{aligned}$$
By [def-weil-endofunctor-fixed-pair-category], this proves that $\varepsilon_M$ is a morphism $\widetilde L\widetilde R(M,\psi)\to(M,\psi)$.
